      "sha256": "fe1c697ffe90e9e672cdae68f8e06493c6cc83bf4c6d2e80dc28c0fa4cc82c24",
      "tokens": [
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 1,
          "text": "NEP-0000 · The NEP Process",
          "id": "nep-0000--the-nep-process"
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "NEP"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": 0000"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Title"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": The NEP Process"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Author"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": SuperNovae Studio maintainers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Status"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": Active · "
              },
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "DORMANT until the v1 pre-freeze"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " (process NEP · never Final)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Type"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": Process"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Created"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": 2026-07-18"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "quote",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "strong",
              "text": "Dormant, and this is what wakes it: the pre-freeze of the language\nat v1."
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " A proposal process only has meaning against something FROZEN.\nBefore the freeze there is nothing to propose "
            },
            {
              "k": "em",
              "text": "against"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " — a new law is\nwritten "
            },
            {
              "k": "strong",
              "text": "directly"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " into "
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "`spec/`",
              "href": "../spec/"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": ", and the deep breaks live\ninside "
            },
            {
              "k": "code",
              "text": "v1"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " itself. On 2026-08-13 the twenty Standards-Track drafts\nwere resolved on exactly that reading: eighteen became the language,\ntwo were never built and are buried as such, and\n"
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "`README.md`",
              "href": "README.md"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " records where each one went."
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "This process becomes load-bearing at the pre-freeze, when every change\nis a proposal again — the maintainers included. "
            },
            {
              "k": "strong",
              "text": "An `Active` status\nwith zero open proposals is not a dead ceremony: it is a mechanism\nwaiting on a named trigger."
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " That sentence is here because a reader\nconcluded the opposite in under an hour, and a clause that says why it\nsleeps beats a status you have to guess."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 2,
          "text": "Abstract",
          "id": "abstract"
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "A NEP (Nika Enhancement Proposal) is the public, numbered document through\nwhich every evolution of the Nika standard is proposed, discussed and\ndecided. This document defines the process itself: the lifecycle, the\ntemplate, who decides, and how the process evolves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "strong",
              "text": "Pre-ratification clause."
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " Until "
            },
            {
              "k": "code",
              "text": "1.0.0"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " ratifies the language, the\nspec on "
            },
            {
              "k": "code",
              "text": "main"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " is the draft and the draft evolves directly — so this era\nopens "
            },
            {
              "k": "strong",
              "text": "no"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " Standards Track NEP: a law is written into "
            },
            {
              "k": "code",
              "text": "spec/"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " where it\nbelongs, and the numbers already spent stay load-bearing in engine code\nand traces (see "
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "`README.md`",
              "href": "README.md"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " for what each resolves to).\n"
            },
            {
              "k": "strong",
              "text": "From the pre-freeze on, this process is binding"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": ": nobody amends the\nstandard directly, the maintainers included."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "The lineage is deliberate: "
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "PEP 1",
              "href": "https://peps.python.org/pep-0001/"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "\ngoverns Python this way, the\n"
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "KEP process",
              "href": "https://github.com/kubernetes/enhancements/blob/master/keps/sig-architecture/0000-kep-process/README.md"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "\ngoverns Kubernetes (itself taken from Rust's RFCs, themselves shaped by\nPEPs), and the "
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "TC39 stages",
              "href": "https://tc39.es/process-document/"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " govern\nJavaScript. A standard earns trust when its evolution has one public door."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 2,
          "text": "Motivation",
          "id": "motivation"
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "Three effects, proven by the processes above:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Credible neutrality."
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " A third-party vendor proposes an evolution\nthrough the same door the maintainers use. That is the condition for\nrival runtimes to adopt the spec at all."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Fork resistance."
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " Fragmentation, relicensing, capture and dialects\nshare one antidote: a public evolution process nobody can confiscate."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "A navigable freeze."
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " Post-1.0 the surface is frozen, additive only.\nWithout a proposal process, frozen means dead. With one, frozen means\nstable and governed: the NEP is the vehicle of every legal addition."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 2,
          "text": "Specification",
          "id": "specification"
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 3,
          "text": "Lifecycle",
          "id": "lifecycle"
        },
        {
          "k": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "Draft → Discussion → Accepted | Rejected → Implemented → Final"
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Draft"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": a PR adding "
              },
              {
                "k": "code",
                "text": "governance/nep-NNNN-<slug>.md"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " from the template.\nThe number is the next free integer, claimed by the PR itself."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Discussion"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": public, in the PR and its linked issue. There is no\nprivate track."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Accepted / Rejected"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": decided per the Decision authority below.\nA rejected NEP stays published with its rationale. The record of noes\nis worth as much as the record of yeses: it prevents relitigating."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Implemented"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": the reference engine ships it behind a green\nconformance suite, and the spec text is amended by the NEP's cascade."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Final"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": the amendment is part of the frozen surface. Process NEPs\n(like this one) stay "
              },
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Active"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " instead: they may be amended by a\nsuccessor NEP."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 3,
          "text": "Types",
          "id": "types"
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Standards Track"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": changes the language surface, the stdlib contract,\nthe conformance suite or the trace format."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Process"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": changes how Nika evolves (this document is one)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Informational"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": records a design position without changing anything."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 3,
          "text": "Decision authority",
          "id": "decision-authority"
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "Today: the SuperNovae Studio maintainers, by explicit written acceptance\nin the NEP's PR. Tomorrow: when three to five independent vendors ship\nconformant runtimes, authority transfers to a technical committee they\nseat together. That transfer is itself a Process NEP, proposed through\nthis same door."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 3,
          "text": "Numbering and the founding era",
          "id": "numbering-and-the-founding-era"
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "NEP numbering runs through this door from NEP-0000 onward, and a number\nis spent for good — the twenty folded on 2026-08-13 are not recycled.\nThe pre-1.0 rulings are the founding era: their verbatim record (the\nRULINGS documents and the ADR line) remains canonical history, not\nretroactive NEPs. One retroactive exception is reserved: NEP-0001,\n\"the nika: v1 language surface\", a Standards Track summary of the\nconstitution as frozen at 1.0, so the language has one readable front\ndoor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 3,
          "text": "Relationship to conformance",
          "id": "relationship-to-conformance"
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "An accepted Standards Track NEP is not Implemented until the conformance\nsuite proves it. The public claim « Nika v1 Conformant — "
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "<Level>"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "\n(spec "
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "<commit>"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": ") » (the one claim string ·\n"
            },
            {
              "k": "link",
              "text": "spec/07 §Claiming conformance",
              "href": "../spec/07-conformance.md#claiming-conformance"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": ")\nis earned by passing the suite, never by declaration. A NEP that cannot\nstate its conformance test does not leave Discussion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "The ratchet is same-PR: an Accepted Standards Track NEP lands its\nconformance fixtures in the implementing PR — the spec text amendment,\nthe registered error codes, and the fixtures that prove them arrive\ntogether, never separately. A registered error code without a fixture\nis a spec bug. (The precedent: MCP made a conformance scenario a\nFinal-gate for every SEP — SEP-2484; this door holds the same bar.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 3,
          "text": "What a NEP is not",
          "id": "what-a-nep-is-not"
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "Not a bug report: defects in the engine go to the engine tracker."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "Not documentation: docs follow the spec, they do not amend it."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "Not a fork of authority: a NEP the maintainers (today) or the committee\n(tomorrow) rejected does not become a dialect. Divergent runtimes lose\nthe compatibility claim per the conformance rule."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 2,
          "text": "How to propose",
          "id": "how-to-propose"
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "Copy "
              },
              {
                "k": "code",
                "text": "governance/nep-template.md"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": " to "
              },
              {
                "k": "code",
                "text": "governance/nep-NNNN-<slug>.md"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "\n(next free number)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "Fill every section. \"Rejected alternatives\" and \"Compatibility impact\"\nare mandatory: an empty alternatives section means the design was not\nexplored."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": "Open the PR. Discussion happens there. Silence is not consent: a NEP\nadvances only by explicit acceptance."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 2,
          "text": "Rejected alternatives",
          "id": "rejected-alternatives"
        },
        {
          "k": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "GitHub issues as the process"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": issues have no lifecycle, no template\ndiscipline, and vanish from the reading order. A numbered file in git\nis citable forever."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "RFC-style mailing list"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": the studio is small and the audience is\ndeveloper-first. The PR is where the diff and the debate share a page."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "k": "strong",
                "text": "Waiting until vendors exist to define the process"
              },
              {
                "k": "text",
                "text": ": the process must\npredate its first external user, or the first external proposal arrives\nwith no door to knock on. Foundations land before the peak."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "k": "h",
          "depth": 2,
          "text": "Compatibility impact",
          "id": "compatibility-impact"
        },
        {
          "k": "p",
          "inline": [
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": "None. This NEP is additive: it creates "
            },
            {
              "k": "code",
              "text": "governance/"
            },
            {
              "k": "text",
              "text": " and binds nothing\nretroactively. The pre-1.0 gate (rulings, migrations, conformance work)\nproceeds unchanged."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
